MarketWeft original code and generated example prices are distributed under 0BSD.
The policy is based on complete SPDX expressions. At least one approved branch of
an OR must be available. Every license in an AND must be satisfied.

Browser distribution
--------------------
Preserve THIRD-PARTY.txt and rust-library-notices.html alongside the compiled
browser assets. The first file contains the installed production npm package
notices. The second is the Rust toolchain's standard-library copyright and
license inventory. OS-provided fonts and WebViews are system components.

Native desktop and development tools
------------------------------------
The desktop wrapper is a separate Cargo workspace. Its Tauri graph contains
the MIT-licensed glib 0.18.5 source with a Debian backport of an upstream
iterator fix. Its original LICENSE and COPYRIGHT files are in
apps/desktop/vendor/glib-0.18.5. Exact provenance is in docs/native-advisories.md.
The desktop dependency graph also contains
unmodified MPL-2.0 files in cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext
and selectors. The web build uses the unmodified MPL-2.0 lightningcss tool and
its platform bindings. These file-scoped terms apply to the respective packages.
No MPL package enters the financial crate or the browser's npm runtime graph.
The policy also accepts the permissive Zlib and Unicode-3.0 terms and the
Apache-2.0 license with the LLVM exception. For dual-licensed packages select
an approved permissive branch. Preserve the terms of each required license.

The Python research wheel uses the MIT-licensed setuptools build backend.
Its version and PyPI wheel digest are pinned in
packages/python-research/build-requirements.txt and included in the inventory.
The installed SDK uses the Python standard library.
Upstream distribution: https://pypi.org/project/setuptools/84.2.1/

The standalone Linux x64 research service includes the original notices from
its Cargo dependencies and the compiler's standard-library copyright inventory.
Keep the notices directory together with the executable.

The Linux x64 research OCI archive includes the pinned Debian base and its
system package notices. The service's notices are installed under
/usr/share/doc/marketweft-research in the image.

docs/dependencies.cdx.json lists exact package versions, integrity digests and
declared licenses, including optional target packages. Rust package source
archives are available at https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/NAME/VERSION/download.
npm source distributions are identified by their resolved URLs in package-lock.json.
Supply corresponding source for any distributed MPL-covered files and retain
all upstream notices. Before shipping a native installer, assemble the native
dependency notices, system-library terms, corresponding source information and
signing evidence for that target. This milestone ships a source wrapper.

To check the inventory, install the locked npm tree, fetch all Cargo
workspaces with cargo fetch --locked, and run python scripts/supply_chain.py
--check from the repository root. Omit --check to regenerate after reviewing a
lockfile change. License gates fail closed for unknown required terms.
